            <ArticleTitle>[Amaurosis fugax of cardiac origin].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>307-16</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 49 year old woman who was admitted to the emergency department for dyspnoea, transient amaurosis and limbs oedema. During hospitalisation a full workup revealed multisystemic thrombosis and dilated cardiomyopathy in relation with viral myocarditis due to Coxackie B infection. Diagnosis and treatment will be discussed in light of the litterature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
